🍷 2️⃣ Wine Type Classification

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Problem Statement

Classify wine into:

* Type 0
* Type 1
* Type 2

Based on chemical properties.

---

🎯 Goal

👉 Classification Problem
👉 Multi-class classification

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📊 Input Features

```text
Alcohol
Malic Acid
Ash
Magnesium
Flavanoids
Color Intensity
Proline
...
```

---

🧠 ML Approach

* Data normalization
* ANN classifier
* Softmax output

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔄 Workflow

```text
Dataset
   ↓
Preprocessing
   ↓
Train-Test Split
   ↓
ANN Model
   ↓
Evaluation (Accuracy, Confusion Matrix)
```

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚙️ TensorFlow Implementation

```python
from tensorflow import keras

model = keras.Sequential([
    keras.layers.Dense(64, activation='relu', input_shape=(13,)),
    keras.layers.Dense(32, activation='relu'),
    keras.layers.Dense(3, activation='softmax')
])

model.compile(
    optimizer='adam',
    loss='sparse_categorical_crossentropy',
    metrics=['accuracy']
)

model.fit(X_train, y_train, epochs=20)
```

---

📊 Evaluation Metrics

* Accuracy
* Precision
* Recall
* F1-score

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔥 PyTorch Implementation (Basic)

```python
import torch
import torch.nn as nn

class WineModel(nn.Module):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(13, 64)
        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(64, 32)
        self.fc3 = nn.Linear(32, 3)
        self.relu = nn.ReLU()

    def forward(self, x):
        x = self.relu(self.fc1(x))
        x = self.relu(self.fc2(x))
        x = self.fc3(x)
        return x
```

